    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. quick follow up, regarding the beam sizing—if i'm spacing my posts every 6 feet instead of 4, what are the main risks of structural failure i should look out for? i want to make sure the whole thing doesn't sag or collapse under heavy use.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When spacing posts 6 feet apart instead of the standard 4 feet, you'll need to be extra cautious of beam sag, deflection, and uneven loading due to increased span lengths. Because the beams will span more distance, they'll be more susceptible to exceeding the tri-phasic bending load resistance capacity (serviceability limit state) and to sagging when completing loads. This could lead to uneven decking surfaces or collapsing under heavy use.",
      "source": "target",
